      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "CONTEXT",
          "content": "The difficult management of chronic daily headache and the lack of clinical trials for this medical condition led the authors to perform this study. Gabapentin has been successfully used for a variety of chronic pain conditions and therefore may be of use in the treatment of chronic headache."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To assess the efficacy and safety of low doses of gabapentin in cases of chronic daily headache."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "DESIGN",
          "content": "Open-label study on a series of cases of chronic daily headache."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "PATIENTS",
          "content": "Twenty-one consecutive patients with primary headache lasting 4 or more hours a day, at least 15 days per month, were invited to participate in this open trial. They were treated with low doses of gabapentin for sufficient time to lead to a headache-free period of at least 7 consecutive days. A minimum of 1 follow-up visit and 1 phone call were made in the subsequent 6-9 months."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "MEASUREMENTS",
          "content": "A simple \"Patient Impression of Change\" was used to evaluate the results. Patients were also invited to compare this treatment to previous ones, whenever possible."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "The efficacy of the treatment with gabapentin was rated as \"excellent\" by 19% of the patients, \"good\" by 47.6%, \"fair\" by 19%, and \"poor\" by 14.4%."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "Despite the inherent limitations of such a small open trial, the authors concluded that ratings of excellent and good by two thirds of this population of patients with chronic daily headache should encourage the setup of a large double-blind, multicentric, placebo-controlled trial of low doses of gabapentin for chronic daily headache."
        }
      ]},
